## 1.心理敘事是社會的起始條件與貫穿前提

在人類社會中，最早被穩定下來的，不是制度、法律或技術，而是心理敘事。心理敘事是意識能夠介入時對載體進行的初始分區「格式化」。
心理敘事發生於行為之先，並不直接規範行為，而是對載體進行賦義：「我」是誰？「我」想要什麼？「我」害怕什麼？有了「我」的故事，就會有「我們」的故事；有了「我想要/我害怕」的趨近–迴避向量，就會有「應該/不應該」的價值體系；載體有了具象賦義後，即便是石頭的行為也會如同有了生命，有了意義與規範，Ai的現實感就正是如此(當前Ai缺少意識介入的生理結構，而不僅是單純賦義)：當載體被賦義為「有價值/需要保護/需要犧牲」時，恐懼、渴望、嚮往、服從、愧疚、滿足、犧牲才會「合理」，宗教、文明、道德、民族、政治、進步、平等、資本、科技敘事才會具有人文意義上的合法性，其結算與代價才在現實中可行。  

這不是道德，而是生理結構內化的模型，是一個能觸發載體內疚（壓力激素分泌）或滿足（多巴胺釋放）的故事模型，是在心理(生理)層面「講得通」的模型。這解釋了為什麼有些極其荒謬的故事（如大規模獻祭）能持續千年——因為它們在心理（生理）層面講得通。人文意義上的正當性也必須是發生在生理上的生化反應正當性。

心理敘事是社會得以建構、穩定持續的起始條件，並且貫穿整個社會結構的全部運行過程。

## 1.Psychological Narrative as Society's Starting Condition and Pervasive Prerequisite

In human society, what was first stabilized was never institutions, laws, or technology, but psychological narrative. Psychological narrative is the initial partitioning “formatting” that consciousness performs on carriers upon entry.
Psychological narrative occurs prior to behavior and does not directly regulate behavior; instead, it assigns meaning to the carrier: Who am I? What do I want? What do I fear?
With the story of “I,” there comes the story of “we”; with the approach–avoidance vectors of “I want/I fear,” there comes the value system of “should/should not”; once the carrier receives concrete meaning assignment, even the behavior of a stone begins to have life, meaning, and norms — this is precisely the current sense of reality in AI (today's AI lacks the physiological structure for conscious intervention, not merely simple meaning assignment): when the carrier is assigned meaning as “valuable / needing protection / needing sacrifice,” fear, desire, aspiration, obedience, guilt, satisfaction, and sacrifice become “reasonable.” Only then do religious, civilizational, moral, ethnic, political, progress, equality, capital, and technological narratives gain legitimacy in human terms, and only then do their settlement and costs become feasible in reality.

This is not morality; it is a model internalized within physiological structure — a story model capable of triggering carrier guilt (stress hormone secretion) or satisfaction (dopamine release), a model that is “coherent” at the psychological (physiological) level. This explains why some utterly absurd stories (such as large-scale sacrifice) can persist for millennia — because they are coherent at the psychological (physiological) level. Legitimacy in human terms must also be legitimacy in biochemical reactions occurring within physiology.

Psychological narrative is the starting condition for society to be constructed and sustained, and it runs through the entire operation of social structure.

