## 3.預設了起始立場的心理敘事：人性本善或人性本惡

對於載體本身立場而言，「性善或性惡」是不是科學結論並沒有多麼重要，重要的是載體的天性決定了需要找一個樣本來「學」。因此，對於介入者意識而言，提供什麼樣的起始立場來講好故事，就顯得格外重要：即要有利於顯化又不能過度消耗載體而終局。現實表明，人性本善或人性本惡的起始的立場設置，能穩定心理秩序、降低不確定性、壓制群體恐懼，在人類社會中取得了極大的成功。

人類自我心理的生理時空邏輯，這一關鍵期在2~3歲前就已經基本完成，是在「學」的需求中通過「從眾/認同」的生理結構，被意識介入賦義參與下的，與所在文化氛圍中的「現實樣本」交互的結果。在這一階段，其自我傾向性、嚮往指向性具有了與現實相關的意義，比如：內/外、大/小、多/少、冷/熱、有/無、先/後，然而，好/坏、善/惡、是/非、利/害等道德價值仍然無法獲得具體賦義，盡管如此，載體在接下來的生命活動過程中，其周圍被「學」樣本的道德價值傾向性，使得載体會類比選擇，相信人性本善或相信人性本惡的敘事立場，這也是作為人的載體融入社會、有意識記忆的開始。

若預設「人性本善」，那麼問題來自外部干擾、制度缺陷，運行邏輯為：我/你/他天生純潔、善良、有潛力，只是被環境/制度/他人污染。
例如：孟子性善論、盧梭「高貴的野蠻人」、浪漫主義、某些現代心理學「自我實現」理論。
此時，「我」往往需要反抗外部結構，以「去除污染」「回歸本性」「解放外界」為代價，支付「追求純潔/反對污染」的心理稅時，理所當然的會產生出向外的仇恨、排他、破壞情節。
若預設「人性本惡」，那麼外界的控制、懲罰、犧牲就具有心理正當性，運行邏輯是：我/你/他天生有缺陷、危害、欠債，需要外部規訓/救贖/控制才能成為「好人」。
例如：原罪、業力、野蠻本能、霍布斯「人人對人人的戰爭」。
此時，「我」必須持續「懺悔、勞動、獻祭」來抵償「本惡」帶來的債務，支付「自我審查/贖罪」的心理稅對意識而言，這就是低成本的、具備「自我監控功能」的穩定群體。

人性本善與人性本惡被預設為敘事的起始立場，也就成為了心理活動的起始立場，在現實中，它已固化成為了意識共識場，一種集體潛意識，這意味著它被廣泛地強制成為了人生觀、價值觀的前置邏輯，後續的所有解釋也都因此自洽展開，現實的人文、道德敘事也因此而具有了意義。它還意味著會強制產生社會結算壓力，讓載體不僅在為生存付費，還在長期為這份「預設立場」付費。

人性本善與人性本惡的敘事，並不是在解釋人性，而是讓人接受自身處境；人類當前的社會處境，也許還可以嘗試新的起始立場，或許，真的已經到了更換立場的時候了。

## 3.Psychological Narrative with Preset Starting Positions: Human Nature Inherently Good or Evil

From the perspective of the carrier itself, whether “human nature is inherently good or evil” is a scientific conclusion is not particularly important. What matters is that the carrier's natural capacity requires finding a sample to “learn” from. Therefore, for the intervening consciousness, providing a starting position that tells a compelling story becomes especially crucial: it must facilitate manifestation while avoiding excessive consumption of the carrier leading to an early end. Reality shows that setting the starting position as human nature inherently good or evil can stabilize psychological order, reduce uncertainty, suppress collective fear, and has achieved tremendous success in human society.

The physiological spatiotemporal logic of human self-psychology is largely completed in the critical period before 2–3 years of age. This occurs through the physiological structure of “conformity/identification” driven by the need to “learn,” with consciousness intervening in meaning assignment and participating in interactions with “real samples” in the surrounding cultural atmosphere. At this stage, the carrier's self-tendencies and aspiration directions acquire meanings related to reality, such as inner/outer, large/small, more/less, cold/hot, presence/absence, before/after. However, moral values such as good/bad, good/evil, right/wrong, benefit/harm still cannot receive concrete meaning assignment. Nevertheless, in subsequent life activities, the moral value tendencies of the “learned” samples surrounding the carrier lead it to analogically choose and believe in narratives of human nature inherently good or evil. This is also the beginning of the carrier, as a human, integrating into society and developing conscious memory.

If “human nature is inherently good” is preset, then problems come from external interference and institutional defects, with the operating logic: I/you/he is innately pure, good, and full of potential, merely polluted by environment/institutions/others.
Examples: Mencius's theory of innate goodness, Rousseau's “noble savage,” Romanticism, certain modern psychological theories of “self-actualization.”
At this point, “I” often needs to resist external structures, paying the psychological tax of “pursuing purity / opposing pollution” at the cost of “removing contamination / returning to nature / liberation,” which naturally generates outward hatred, exclusion, and destructive impulses.

If “human nature is inherently evil” is preset, then external control, punishment, and sacrifice gain psychological legitimacy, with the operating logic: I/you/he is innately defective, harmful, indebted, requiring external discipline/redemption/control to become a “good person.”
Examples: original sin, karma, savage instincts, Hobbes's “war of all against all.”
At this point, “I” must continuously “repent, labor, sacrifice” to repay the debt brought by “inherent evil,” paying the psychological tax of “self-censorship / atonement.” For consciousness, this is a low-cost, stable group with built-in “self-monitoring” function.

Human nature inherently good or evil, preset as the starting position of narrative, becomes the starting position of psychological activity. In reality, it has solidified into the consensus field of consciousness — a collective unconscious. This means it is widely and forcibly imposed as the prerequisite logic for worldview and values, with all subsequent explanations unfolding coherently as a result, giving real humanistic and moral narratives their meaning. It also means it forcibly generates social settlement pressure, making carriers pay not only for survival but also long-term for this “preset position.”

Narratives of human nature inherently good or evil are not explaining human nature; they are enabling people to accept their own circumstances. Perhaps humanity's current social circumstances can still attempt a new starting position — perhaps the time has truly come to change positions.

