## 5.Nationalism: The Most Powerful Psychological Cohesion Narrative Tool in History

Nationalism is a narrative construction by consciousness, targeting the carrier's natural capacities and driven by conformity/identification as the motive force, through a meaning transfer that converts individual settlements — such as suffering, death, or glory — into collective glory through identification. It maximizes the satisfaction of the psychological demand for conformity, making nationalism the narrative in social structure with the strongest psychological cohesion, lowest cost, most direct effect, highest efficiency, and greatest persistence.
The narrative operation of nationalism successfully convinces carriers of its sacredness: one's own poverty, disability, or even death can be transformed into “glory” for the virtual entity of “nation”; making “voluntary suffering,” “glorious dedication,” “perseverance through illness,” and “endurance of hardship” become necessary virtues within the system — painful yet beautiful — voluntarily paying resources, bodies, and lives for this “nation” story: even if physical life is lost, “eternal life” is gained within the narrative.

Religious narrative is a typical application of nationalism, draping it in a “sacred garment”: we are not random aggregates, but a group chosen by God/Heavenly Dao. Individual fear gains a collective object, individual suffering gains collective explanation and dilution, and sacrifice is no longer loss but value accumulation in a higher story. Collective rituals such as sacrifice, prayer, taboos, pilgrimage, and holy war promote group consistency requirements, allowing carriers to continuously confirm “I belong to this story” through intentional or unconscious repetitive behavior.
Similarly, any nation or group that can tell a good conformity/identification story naturally possesses cohesion and centripetal force. Identity politics further subdivides carriers, reallocating Quanli relationships through the creation of microscopic “identification conflicts,” confirming and refining group cohesion.

Any entity that can tell a good “conformity + identification” story — no matter what it is — becomes the psychological foundation for the legitimacy and rationality of any form of good/evil, custom, religion, group, national righteousness, state power, and their behaviors — this is physiologically determined by the natural mechanism starting from “learning.”MAGA is the classic specimen of contemporary nationalism: Roosevelt told this story in his time, Hitler told this story, Trump is telling it today, and Chinese culture has been telling it continuously, never interrupted.

