## 6.幸存者偏差：社會統計學中的敘事幻覺

幸存者敘事，是統計與數據時代的現代社會中常見的、卻也最隱蔽的「從眾+認同」的敘事，是披上了科學外衣的民族主義變體，它給載體提供了「中獎幻覺」。
「幸存者的經驗→走到最後的人證明了道路正確→能適應的留下來了」，這些敘事，都可以是真實的、現實的、統計學成立的、極具說服力的故事，如成功人士、贏家、英雄，但這還不够，即便全部都是統計學確認真實的，相信它們也並不等效於追逐它們。然而民族主義的精髓「賦義轉移」的群體歸類來了：只要你還努力，你也可以象他們一樣。努力，是人人都能輕鬆伸手够到的，而「你還不夠努力」却是無法承受的群體排斥，何況支付勞動、時間、健康就有「可期回報」的投資呢~
但被淘汰的、崩潰的、沉默的、退出的絕大多數，並不在樣本之中；「不可見者」死亡、破產、畸形、精神崩潰被結構性隱形；完全真實的，其路徑也通常會是不可複製的，個體差異是現實無法逾越的鴻溝。

幸存者敘事是意識最常用的信用擴張工具，其隱形了絕大多數崩潰、畸形、精神失常的樣本，是維持社會信用體系不發生連鎖擠兌的重要手段；倖存者敘事本質上是現代社會的鎮痛劑，它將殘酷的社會篩選轉譯成了一場看似形式公平的遊戲，以溫和的外在形式，隱藏極其殘酷的本質：失敗者在承受物理痛苦的同時，還要承擔「不夠努力」的心理羞恥感。

幸存者敘事看似在「鼓勵成功」，實際是「延後崩潰」。

## 6.Survivorship Bias: Narrative Illusion in Social Statistics

Survivorship narrative is one of the most common yet most concealed forms of “conformity + identification” narrative in modern society of the statistical and data era. It is a variant of nationalism cloaked in scientific garb, providing carriers with the “lottery-winning illusion.”
“The experience of survivors → those who made it to the end prove the path is correct → those who adapted survived.” These narratives can be real, factual, statistically valid, and highly persuasive stories, such as successful individuals, winners, heroes. But that alone is not enough; even if they are all statistically confirmed as true, believing in them does not equate to chasing them. Yet the core of nationalism — the meaning transfer through group categorization — arrives: as long as you keep trying hard, you can be like them. Effort is something everyone can easily reach for, while “you are not trying hard enough” is an unbearable group exclusion. Moreover, investing labor, time, and health comes with the promise of “expected returns.”
Yet the vast majority who were eliminated, collapsed, silenced, or withdrew are not in the sample; the “invisible ones” — death, bankruptcy, deformity, mental breakdown — are structurally rendered invisible. Even when fully real, their paths are usually non-replicable; individual differences are an insurmountable chasm in reality.

Survivorship narrative is consciousness's most commonly used tool for credit expansion. It renders invisible the vast majority of collapse, deformity, and mental breakdown cases, serving as an important mechanism to prevent chain runs on the social credit system. In essence, survivorship narrative is the analgesic of modern society: it translates brutal social screening into what appears to be a formally fair game. With a gentle outer form, it conceals an extremely cruel essence: while the failures bear physical suffering, they must also shoulder the psychological shame of “not trying hard enough.”

Survivorship narrative appears to “encourage success,” but in reality it is “postponing collapse.”

