## 7.The Reality That Psychological Narrative Must Confront

The asymmetrical structure between consciousness and carriers is an unavoidable reality: consciousness desires unlimited expansion, while the carrier's real bearing capacity is finite, creating an irreconcilable contradiction between the two. Consciousness can endlessly trial-and-error and issue narrative credit; the carrier, however, is disposable hardware—structural damage is irreversible.

Psychological narrative has become a core component of social structure. It not only drives life and production but also provides遮蔽 reasons and rationalized excuses for carrier overload, collapse, and structural destruction. Yet the carrier is the only stable anchor for consciousness to intervene in reality. This requires consciousness to lower its arrogant head and confront the reality of structural damage to the carrier.

In eras of low productivity, psychological narrative tended toward “delayed gratification” (for heaven, for descendants, for the other shore). In modern times, with the steady rise in productivity levels, psychological narrative has shifted toward “immediate excitement” (for dopamine, likes, consumer pleasure). The carrier's “settlement cycle” has been drastically shortened, leaving neural structures in a state of continuous high-frequency consumption, accelerating structural fragility. Psychological collapse states characterized by anxiety, depression, dissociation, and compulsion are becoming widespread. This large-scale depression is essentially the carrier's psychological compensation (identification, success, future expectations) failing to offset the physical quota being extracted in reality, leading to identification crisis and forced activation of “circuit-breaker protection,” manifesting as low desire and depression.

With the development of science and technology, increasingly efficient productivity levels also mean increasingly efficient destruction technology levels. Thus, irremediable structural destruction in reality will inevitably occur at an accelerating pace.
Evidently, the AGI race represented by accelerationism already presumes it can ignore carriers and expand infinitely. This story will ultimately end due to the loss of “hardware support.”

